Kubernetes Python Application Troubleshooting & Deployment
This repository documents the resolution of a Kubernetes deployment and service misconfiguration issue involving a Python Flask application (poroko/flask-demo-app), ensuring high availability, correct container image referencing, and proper traffic routing via NodePort.

📋 Problem Statement
During the deployment of a Python application on the Kubernetes cluster, the application pods failed to start and traffic could not reach the container successfully. The objectives were to:

Fix the image pull error on the deployment named python-deployment-devops.

Ensure the correct application image (poroko/flask-demo-app) is utilized.

Configure the Kubernetes Service (python-service-devops) with a nodePort of 32345 and a targetPort matching the Flask app's default port (5000).

🛠️ Troubleshooting & Resolution Workflow
1. Diagnosing Deployment Issues
By inspecting the deployment and pods, we discovered an ImagePullBackOff status caused by a typo in the image name:

Bash
kubectl get deployments
kubectl get pods
kubectl describe deployment python-deployment-devops
Error Identified: The deployment was referencing poroko/flask-app-demo instead of the required poroko/flask-demo-app.

2. Inspecting and Correcting the Service Configuration
Checking the existing service revealed that the targetPort and port mappings were targeting port 8080 instead of Flask's default port (5000):

Bash
kubectl describe service python-service-devops
3. Applying the Corrected Manifests
We defined and applied an updated, clean service configuration using kubectl apply:

YAML
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: python-service-devops
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: python_app
  ports:
  - port: 8080
    targetPort: 5000
    nodePort: 32345
Applied via:

Bash
kubectl apply -f service.yaml --force
📸 Previews & Verification
Verified Service Configuration
Running kubectl describe service python-service-devops confirmed that traffic correctly maps to the default Flask application port with the required NodePort:

Plaintext
Name:                     python-service-devops
Namespace:                default
Selector:                 app=python_app
Type:                     NodePort
Port:                     8080/TCP
TargetPort:               5000/TCP
NodePort:                 32345/TCP
Endpoints:                10.22.0.10:5000
